---
import CollectionTopics from "../../components/CollectionTopics.astro";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import trial from "../../../../docs/expansion-measurements/2026-11-21/materials.json";
---
<Base collection="materials" landing title="Materials Science collection — TrendBio" canonicalPath="/collections/materials/"
  description="A cross-field reading collection on heat transport and polymer flow, with original research from physics, chemistry and engineering.">
  <article>
    <p class="collection-date">Seven selected papers from <time>{trial.start}</time> to <time>{trial.end}</time>. The groups below are reading selections.</p>
    <CollectionTopics field="materials" label="Materials Science" groups={trial.groups} />
    <details id="sources"><summary>Sources and selection</summary>
      <p>The four-week source pool contained {Object.entries(trial.sources).map(([source,count]) => `${count} from ${source}`).join(", ")}. We matched arXiv identifiers across versions, DOIs, declared version links and normalized titles, leaving {trial.distinct.toLocaleString("en-US")} distinct records. Unlinked versions with different titles can remain.</p>
      <p>We selected original studies from multiple weeks whose abstracts address the same material property. Dates are first submissions on arXiv and publication dates for journals. The collection has no scheduled ranking.</p>
    </details>
    <p>Related editions · <a href="/physics-expanded/">Expanded Physics</a> · <a href="/chemistry/">Chemistry</a> · <a href="/engineering/">Engineering</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .collection-date { margin-block-end: .5rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--t3); }
  summary { cursor: pointer; }
  details + p { margin-top: 1rem; }
</style>
